## Abstract

Recent advances in AI-based weather modeling have given rise to large-scale “weather foundation” models pretrained on large amounts of weather data. In this study, we investigate whether the Prithvi weather foundation model pretraining on 40 years of MERRA2 data, characterized by a resolution of 0.5° × 0.625° facilitates adaptation to ERA5, which has a finer resolution of 0.25° × 0.25°. We

